  "id": "Compound::DB01115 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Nifedipine, a well-known calcium channel blocker, is shown to interact with Cyp1a2 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Nifedipine binds to Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, both of which are involved in oxidative metabolism, specifically in the reduction of quinones or similar compounds. These enzymes are then linked to Cyp1a2, indicating a potential pathway where Nifedipine indirectly influences Cyp1a2 through the activation of other cytochrome P450 enzymes. The shared involvement of Cyp1a2 in these metabolic processes suggests a possible role in the biotransformation of xenobiotics, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Nifedipine to Cyp1a2 highlights the complexity of drug-target interactions, emphasizing the need for precise mechanistic validation.",
